-- erwartet: C001
-- **644 -- `embeds … scale N` with an `N` that is wider than every C integer type.**
--
-- An embedded pointer field is a bit range and a multiplier, and the emitter wrote the
-- multiplier into the reader as a literal:
--
--     static inline uint64_t F_rahmen(const F *v) {
--         return (uint64_t)((((uint64_t)gabbro_le64(v->bytes + 0) >> 12) & 1099511627775u)
--                           * 18446744073709551616u); }
--
-- `2^64` has no C type. `cc` said *integer constant is too large for its type*, and the
-- checker said `2 items, 0 errors, 0 hints` about the same file.
--
-- **This was the `konst_zahl` family with the cast repaired and the QUESTION still open.**
-- On 2026-09-02 `emit.rs::konst_zahl` was changed from `Some(*n as i128)` to
-- `i128::try_from(*n).ok()`, which stopped the emitter writing `-1` for `2^128 - 1`. It did
-- not stop it writing `2^64`: that value fits `i128` perfectly well, so `konst_zahl` hands
-- it over, and the next 64 bits of the journey had no owner. *A repair at the reader is not
-- a repair at the writer.*
--
-- THE REPAIR, 2026-09-03 -- the fence stands where the C types end
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- **The honest answer is a named refusal -- the emitter cannot write this number, and
-- `C001` is the sentence for exactly that.** There is nothing being withheld: `unsigned
-- long long` is at least 64 bits wide and C promises no more, so `2^64` has no spelling in
-- any base with any suffix.
--
-- The fence is `u64::try_from` at the point where the multiplier becomes C text, and not
-- one door earlier. *That is the lesson the `i128` cast taught from the other side:* a
-- reader that widens is not a writer that checks, and the only place that can know whether
-- a number fits is the place that writes it down.
--
-- > The same day, the general door got the same fence: `czahl` refuses any literal past
-- > `2^64 - 1` wherever one reaches C, and writes the `u` suffix between `2^63` and
-- > `2^64 - 1` where C needs one (`messung/proben/probe-literal-past-the-signed-end.gab`).
-- > **`scale` needs its own because its number never passes through that door** -- it comes
-- > out of `konst_zahl` as an `i128` and is formatted straight into the reader.

module gift::scale_wider_than_any_c_integer {

format F endian little {
    lo     : u64 @[11:0] reserved,
    rahmen : u64 embeds [51:12] scale 18446744073709551616,
    hi     : u64 @[63:52] reserved,
}

}
